{%- comment -%}
  Record one policy violation for the TOKEN that made the call, in the current slice of
  the rolling abuse window (spec §12.4 abuse tracking; helpers/limits/abuse_window). O(1):
  a single counter (same mechanism as the rate limiter), NOT a ledger scan — the ledger
  remains the audit surface, this is just a cheap tripwire. Called at each violation exit
  in the pipeline (deny, invalid args, unknown tool, rate-limit, rejected approval).

  Counted per token, not per person: limits/enforce_abuse suspends only the token whose
  own count crosses the threshold, so a narrowed token handed to a less-trusted agent
  cannot get the person's other tokens revoked.

  @param {string} principal_id
  @param {string} token_id     - the mcp_token that made the call (auth.token_id)
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/note_violation/build', principal_id: principal_id, token_id: token_id
  # Abuse tracking switched off (window <= 0): nothing to record.
  unless object.enabled
    return true
  endunless
  function object = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/note_violation/check', object: object
  if object.valid
    function _ = 'modules/mcp/commands/limits/note_violation/execute', object: object
  endif
  return true
%}
